  "as_of_notes": "Most recent official Michigan DOS 'Registered Voter Count' report (2025 Voter Registration Totals). The report provides three point-in-time snapshots per year (May, August, November); the most recent column, November 2025, is used here and dated 2025-11-01 per Michigan's first-of-reporting-month convention. statewide_total_registered uses the November 'all registered voters' column (8,260,991), which includes both active and inactive registrations. The November 'active registered voters' total is 7,339,283; per the report footnote, the Active Voter Count excludes voters who have not voted in at least six years or have been sent a Notice Pursuant to MCL 168.509aa. Each county object also carries an 'active_registered' field with the November active count.",
  "data_quality": "high",
  "notes": "Source: official PDF from the Michigan Department of State / Bureau of Elections, derived from the Qualified Voter File (QVF). All 83 counties present. County-level 'all registered' sums to 8,260,991 and 'active' sums to 7,339,283, both matching the report's printed statewide totals exactly. Michigan does not register voters by party, so registers_by_party=false and all by_party fields are null. A newer 2026 report was probed (2026-Registered-Voter-Count.pdf) and returned HTTP 404, confirming the 2025 report is the latest. The live MVIC voter-count page (mvic.sos.state.mi.us/VoterCount) is behind a Cloudflare JS challenge and could not be machine-read; the published PDF is the authoritative, citable source."
